  "key_purpose": "evidence_device",
  "why_this_file_exists": "Quarantine cannot be exercised by a wire artifact under evidence-exchange/v1. The epoch is derived from the key, so two conforming registrations cannot naturally name the same epoch with different keys -- that would require a SHA-256 collision. A registration claiming a held epoch with a different key now fails epoch recomputation first, which is covered by anchor-registration's claimed_epoch_mismatch case. Quarantine remains as a receiver-state invariant against rows that predate recomputation, were migrated, or were corrupted, and that is what this file tests: stored state plus one conforming artifact.",
